<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela to sell Consolidated Insurance June 6.</title>
<headline>Venezuela to sell Consolidated Insurance June 6.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's state Deposits Guarantee Fund Fogade will auction Florida-based insurance company Consolidated Property and Casualty Insurance on May 6 for a base price of $2.5 million, Fogade said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Consolidated passed to Fogade in 1994 as part of guarantees given by Venezuelan bank Banco Consolidado for financial aid during a severe financial sector crisis.</p>
<p>Consolidated had assets of $8.5 million and a net worth of $2.5 million at the end of 1996, Fogade said.</p>
<p>((-- Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
